{title: 255 - I Cannot Tell Why}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Jesus Christ}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[G]I cannot [C/G]tell [G7/F]why He whom [C/G]angels [Am]wor-ship
[F]Should [Am]set His [G7/D]loveupon [C]the souls of [G]men,
[G]Or why as [C/G]Shepherd [G7]He should [C]seek the [Am]wanderers,
[F]To bring them [Em/B]back, [F]they know not how nor when.F]
[Am]But this Iknow, [C]that He was born [Am]of [G7/F]Mary
[C/E]When [B7]Bethlehem’s [Am]manger [C]was [G]His on- [C]lyhome,
[Bdim]And that [Dm]He lived [C]at Nazareth [Am]and la [C]bored;
[G]And so the Savior, [F]Savior of [C/E]the world, [Em]has come.

Verse 2:
[G]I cannot [C/G]tell [G7/F]how silently [C/G]He [Am]suffered
[F]As [Am]with His [G7/D]peace [C]He graced this place of [G]tears,
[G]Nor how His [C/G]heart [G7/F]upon the [C]cross was [Am]broken,
[F]The crown of [Em/B]pain [F]to three and thirty years.
[Am]But this I [C]know He heals the broken [G7/F]hearted
[C/E]And [B7]stays [Am]our sin and [C]calms our [G]lurking [Em]fear,
[Bdim]And lifts [Dm]the burden [C/E]from [F#dim]the heavy [Am]laden;
[G]For still the Savior, [F]Savior of [C/E]the world, [Em]is here.

Verse 3:
[G]I cannot [C/G]tell [G7/F]how He will [C/G]win the [Am]nations,
[F]How [Am]He will [G7/D]claim [C]His earthly heritage,
[G]How satisfy [G7/F]the needs and [C]aspirations
[F]Of east and [Em/B]west, [F]of sinner and of sage.
[Am]But this I [C]know all flesh shall see [Am]His [G7/F]glory,
[C/E]And [B7]He [Am]shall reap the [C]harvest [G]He [C]has [Em]sown,
[Bdim]And some [Dm]glad day [C]His sun [F#dim]will shine [Am]in splendor
[G]When He the Savior, [F]Savior of [C/E]the world, [Em]is known.

Verse 4:
[G]I cannot [C/G]tell [G7/F]how all the [C/G]lands shall [Am]worship,
[F]When [Am]at His [G7/D]bidding [C]every storm is [G]stilled,
[G]Or who can [C/G]say [G7/F]how great the [C]jubilation
[F]When all our [Em/B]hearts [F]with love for Him are filled.
[Am]But this I [C]know the skies shall sound [Am]His [G7/F]praises,
[C/E]Ten [B7]thousand [Am]thousand [C]human [G]voices [Em]sing,
[Bdim]And earth [Dm]to heaven, [C]and heaven [F#dim]to earth [Am]will answer,
[G]At last the Savior, [F]Savior of [C/E]the world, [Em]is King!
